 "input": "debian packaging, how I do mine. watch file notices a new upstream release, I pull the tarball, update debian/changelog. build in a clean chroot with sbuild, run lintian on the result and fix what it complains about. autopkgtest runs the package tests. if all good, sign and dput the upload to the archive. it lands in unstable, then migrates to testing automatically after a few days if no release-critical bugs filed and it builds on all arches (buildds do the other architectures). bugs come in through the BTS, I close them from the changelog entries.",
 "expect_status": "ok",
